      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ZIPPING POPYRIN (3) broke through for his maiden success two back but could manage only midfield last time when finished fourth and beaten 3 lengths at this track over 324m (18.12). Returns to the scene of his maiden win. Will find this more suitable and can atone. ALIRA (1) pinged the lids from out wide but faded out of it late when 6th at Richmond in a Grade 5. Has the ability to give this a shake. SHAMEFUL (8) was safely held last time out, finishing seventh at Richmond over 401m behind Spring Rota (23.55) in a Grade 5. The form from his last run stacks up well. Key runner who gets his chance to atone. ARCHIE'S CHOICE (4) can finish much closer after missing a cheque at this track last start.",
